comment0.target=SlotMachineC2Test
comment0.text=\r\n The test class SlotMachineC2Test.\r\n Pruebas para el Ciclo 2\: Extensiones como swap, lock, unlock, configuraciones por arreglos y pasos de giro.\r\n\r\n @author David Garzon, Wilson Mendivelso\r\n @version 1\r\n
comment1.target=void setUp()
comment1.text=\r\n Sets up the test fixture.\r\n Called before every test case method.\r\n
comment10.target=void shouldUnlockIfWheelPosIsTooShort()
comment10.text=\r\n If wheel position is too short it should unlock the first wheel.\r\n
comment11.target=void shouldUnlockIfWheelPosIsTooBig()
comment11.text=\r\n If wheel position is too big it should unlock the last wheel.\r\n
comment12.target=void shouldSpinBackIfStepsAreNegatives()
comment12.text=\r\n If steps are negative we should spin back.\r\n
comment13.target=void shoultNotSpinIfStepsAreZero()
comment13.text=\r\n If steps are zero it should be at the same place.\r\n
comment14.target=void shouldSpinNPositionsCorrectly()
comment14.text=\r\n If steps are given it should spin correctly.\r\n
comment15.target=void shouldSpinLastWheelIfWheelNumIsTooBig()
comment15.text=\r\n If the number of wheel is too big it will spin the last wheel.\r\n
comment16.target=void shouldSpinFirstWheelIfWheelNumIsTooShort()
comment16.text=\r\n If the number of wheel is too short it will spin the first wheel.\r\n
comment17.target=void shouldSetAllSymbols()
comment17.text=\r\n If symbols are given all the wheels must be in the position of the setSymbols.\r\n
comment18.target=void shouldStayAWheelIfItsSymbolIsIncorrect()
comment18.text=\r\n If there are incorrect symbols, those wheels should ignore the spin.\r\n
comment19.target=void shouldPassFirstAcceptationTest()
comment19.text=\r\n This is the first acceptation test.\r\n
comment2.target=void shouldSwapWheelsWillChangeColorsOrder()
comment2.text=\r\n If we do a swap between two symbols with different colors configuration should change.\r\n
comment20.target=void shouldSecondAcceptationTestPass()
comment20.text=\r\n This is the Second acceptation test.\r\n
comment21.target=void tearDown()
comment21.text=\r\n Tears down the test fixture.\r\n
comment3.target=void shouldNotChangeIfSwapWithTheSameWheel()
comment3.text=\r\n If the swap is with the same wheel it should not change the configuration.\r\n
comment4.target=void shouldSwapIfWheelPosIsTooShort()
comment4.text=\r\n If one of the wheels position is too short we should take the first wheel.\r\n
comment5.target=void shouldSwapIfWheelPosIsTooBig()
comment5.text=\r\n If one of the wheels position is too big we should take the last wheel.\r\n
comment6.target=void shouldNotChangeWheelsSymbolIfItIslocked()
comment6.text=\r\n If a wheel is locked, it should not change the symbols.\r\n
comment7.target=void shouldLockIfWheelPosIsTooShort()
comment7.text=\r\n If wheel position is too short it should lock the first wheel.\r\n
comment8.target=void shouldLockIfWheelPosIsTooBig()
comment8.text=\r\n If wheel position is too big it should lock the last wheel.\r\n
comment9.target=void shouldChangeWheelsSymbolsIfItIsUnlocked()
comment9.text=\r\n If a wheel is unlocked, it can change its symbols.\r\n
